From 5003630ff22a4f5f5745bcfe036c91443774aad1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:41:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] Plugins: this build's own plugins can be removed, and
 added again

Settings' Remove did nothing for a plugin this build ships (data/ct-plugins:
the fork's own plugins and the original's as the fork took them): it tried
to forget a developer folder. Now such a plugin is a reviewed one tagged
"Clicktrough" (not "Dev"); Remove takes it away (the installed copy too)
and keeps it away (dpsMeter.ctPluginsRemoved), and Available lists it to
install again, which brings this build's copy back with its saved data.
One of the original's that runs only where installed is simply uninstalled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RBQati3x8VviBbpY9juEWf
